+/* LanRDP: never use a lone shift key as the client shortcut modifier. FreeRDP defaults to
+ * KMOD_RSHIFT, which swallows ordinary typing on macOS: RShift+D disconnected the session,
+ * RShift+G/R toggled grab/resizable, RShift+M minimized, and the capital letters never
+ * reached the remote desktop. Use Ctrl+Alt instead, which is not part of regular text input.
+ * The mask is compared with (mods & mask) == mask, so list the concrete left-hand keys: the
+ * aggregate KMOD_CTRL/KMOD_ALT values contain both the left and right bit and never match. */
+static const std::vector<std::string> hotkey_default_modmask{ "KMOD_LCTRL", "KMOD_LALT" };
 
